# `genesis/data/rakia` — observed capacity governance

The aggregate binding reads typed `cluster.ratifications` in `compute-capacity.json`: only CPU
limits may exceed allocatable up to the ratified percentage; requests reserve and memory is
incompressible. A ledger older than 30 days refers for refresh without an aggregate-capacity ask,
retaining the underlying violations in the message. Run `k8s-bridge observe --ledger genesis/data/rakia/compute-capacity.json` with
`PROMETHEUS_URL` set (or `--prometheus-url`) to promote a fresh cluster observation.
Use `--dry-run` to review field changes first. Commitments, utilization actuals and ephemeral
storage remain operator-curated; missing or invalid node evidence refuses promotion.
